<title>BELGIUM: Western Europe January car registrations - details.</title>
<headline>Western Europe January car registrations - details.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are provisional West European new car registrations and market share figures for January released on Thursday by the European Automobile Manufacturers Association (ACEA).</p>
<p> Brand		  Jan 97    pct change  pct mkt share vs Jan 96</p>
<p> All brands	   1,130,000   -2.9 pct</p>
<p> Volkswagen	     194,800   -0.1	   17.2	 16.8</p>
<p> Fiat		     146,500   -3.1	   13.0	 13.0</p>
<p> GM			 142,728   -3.8	   12.6	 12.7</p>
<p> Ford		     132,807   -5.2	   11.8	 12.0</p>
<p> Japanese		 121,271   +2.7	   10.7	 10.1</p>
<p> PSA			120,605   -12.3	  10.7	 11.8</p>
<p> Renault		  105,894   -6.4	    9.4	  9.7</p>
<p> BMW			 64,623   -4.0	    5.7	  5.8</p>
<p> Mercedes		  38,700  -11.0	    3.4	  3.7</p>
<p> Volvo		     18,744  +16.6	    1.7	  1.4</p>
<p>(Volkswagen includes Audi, Seat, Skoda. GM includes Opel/Vauxhall, U.S. imports, Saab, IBC/ISUZU. PSA includes Peugeot, Citroen. Fiat includes Lancia, Alfa Romeo, Innocenti, Ferrari, Maserati. Ford includes U.S. imports, Jaguar. BMW includes Rover. Japanese includes Nissan, Toyota, Mazda, Honda, Mitsubishi, other.) - Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
</text>
